+The tool-permission and environment policy a Job is admitted under is
+provider-neutral and shared by every execution of the Job. Each execution's
+provider-specific command and environment configuration is bound to its own
+adapter identity and MUST implement that shared policy. Different provider
+commands are allowed; a different policy or an adapter that does not implement
+it MUST be refused.
+
+
+Owner clarification 2026-11-24: for Jobs under explicit model-attribution
+composition, publication recovery MUST carry and validate the original producing
+attempt's contributor evidence, bound to that attempt and the exact retained
+candidate. The requested model MUST appear in the validated contributor set.
+Missing, conflicting or invalid evidence MUST prevent candidate acceptance and
+handoff to review, with an honest held/refused outcome for the owner; retained
+output remains preserved. A provider-free publication worker transports the
+candidate and MUST NOT replace its producer attribution. Existing legacy
+admissions retain their existing behavior. See the [owner ruling](../work/records/2026/11/finding-v12-native-provider-selection/ASSIGNMENT-N1N2-OWNER-B-2026-11-24.md).
